						<a href="/scp-5870/comments/show">SCP-5870</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4857278">
									

<p>Hello! Veralta's here with a new SCP about koalas, nature, the future of Australia, and intricate worldbuilding based on the beliefs of aboriginal Australian people like the Bundjalung and the Eora. Consider this SCP a free New Year trip through Australia, and a little bit of a crash course on the Australian condition.</p>
<p>Also, it's linked to Ralliston's Obearwatch Command; fun fact, all of these started when he threw the word &quot;Koalalition&quot; at me, and I said, &quot;Hmm&#8230; uwah, this looks interesting&quot;. I initially planned out a short article with a gimmick and a punchline.</p>
<p>But then, I realized I had to dive deep into the waterhole.</p>
<p>The aboriginal Australian belief system, also called Dreamtime<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-695392-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-695392-1')">1</a></sup>, is very complex and interesting. It would be a shame if I just went with a silly punchline when aboriginal culture, with its mix of hopes and dreams for Australia, needs a chance to shine here.</p>
<p>Lastly, consider this article as a piece dedicated to Australians and wildlife - such as the koalas themselves - who have been affected by the severe bushfires. As a Filipino youth, I couldn't do much to be honest, aside from raising awareness. The facts presented in the Background Report are based on my research about the facts collected by Australian orgs themselves, while I tried to stay true to the myths' essence while adding my style of writing to them.</p>
<p>All in all, though, please enjoy this SCP, and I wish a Happy New Year - and more happy years - to come for all of us!</p>
